WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.967
Review the sample workflow: a field checklist and its budget.

2
00:00:03.967 --> 00:00:08.967
Choose a trigger. This example starts only with a manual run.

3
00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:13.933
Check the condition before execution: battery between 20% and 100%.

4
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:18.933
Set, split and join QVars to build the checklist.

5
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:22.933
Run Python, store its output in a QVar, then append it to a vault note.

6
00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:26.933
Inspect the action payload before it runs.

7
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:32.933
Read the Python source, output variable and execution timeout.

8
00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:36.933
Save the reviewed workflow, ready for a manual run.

9
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:41.900
Press Run. The five actions execute in order.

10
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.900
The run succeeds and the vault note is updated.

11
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.867
Open the run log: manual trigger, duration and completed status.

12
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:58.200
Open the saved note: checklist, real Python output and a total of 102 EUR.
